From 15b80c1fbf4e8800e888964055b01565cc56b0f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian <219239532+markd3ng@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 15:03:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] fix(storage): keep original metadata error if claim
 cleanup fails

Context:
Greptile P1 on 0673611 noted that a throwing cleanup R2 PUT masked the original KV metadata failure.

Expected behavior:
Claim cleanup remains best-effort and generation-safe. If that cleanup throws, the original metadata error is still returned.

Acceptance criteria:
- a throwing cleanup PUT still surfaces the original KV failure to the client

Constraints:
- generic upstream behavior only
- do not modify upstream-sync
- dual R2+KV failure remains fail-closed until expiry/cleanup; no reservation namespace

Validation:
- RED: worker/test/writeConcurrency.spec.ts expected "kv unavailable", observed "cleanup put failed"
- GREEN: Node 22 ./node_modules/.bin/vitest run worker/test/writeConcurrency.spec.ts -> 7 passed
- REGRESSION: Node 22 ./node_modules/.bin/vitest run --project Workers -> 17 files, 121 tests passed
- tsc --noEmit and eslint on changed files passed

Docs:
- N/A; public API contract unchanged

Upstream base:
0835cac4ab8f974035d31845f5c2b93b0c85b5c6

Patch ID:
050-atomic-named-paste-create (candidate; verify against refreshed series before export)

Dependencies:
none

Refs:
- https://github.com/Skyline-Gazer/pastebin-worker/issues/78
- https://github.com/Skyline-Gazer/pastebin-worker/pull/99
- Greptile P1 on 0673611: cleanup failure strands claim
